<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>The economic issues and policy in France - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 07:07:29 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>Bayeux Tapestry arrives in Britain in high-security night-time operation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260710-bayeux-tapestry-arrives-in-britain-in-high-security-night-time-operation</link><description>
After almost 1,000 years, the priceless Medieval Bayeux Tapestry is back on English soil – spirited into London's British Museum on Friday in the dead of night, after a high-tech and high-security operation where any slip-up could have spelled disaster.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/22937990-606f-11f1-9b0d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-Tapestry-scene57-Harold-death.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/22937990-606f-11f1-9b0d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-Tapestry-scene57-Harold-death.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14fa8278-7c27-11f1-96b9-e532d0368fe7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 07:06:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/22937990-606f-11f1-9b0d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-Tapestry-scene57-Harold-death.jpg">© Myrabella, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France must speed up climate action as watchdog warns current efforts fall short</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260710-france-must-speed-up-climate-action-as-watchdog-warns-current-efforts-fall-short</link><description>
France is not prepared for the pace and scale of climate change, the country’s climate watchdog warned in a report that calls for a significant acceleration of both emissions reduction efforts and adaptation policies, as the country faces its third heatwave since May.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33118760-7b9c-11f1-95af-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T064201Z-180942209-RC29ILA7EQ9D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-CLIMATE-ADAPTATION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33118760-7b9c-11f1-95af-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T064201Z-180942209-RC29ILA7EQ9D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-CLIMATE-ADAPTATION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6972d9d6-7b9b-11f1-a938-5b9af79f737d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 05:24:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33118760-7b9c-11f1-95af-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T064201Z-180942209-RC29ILA7EQ9D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-CLIMATE-ADAPTATION.jpg">© Alice Sacco/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Secrecy surrounds Bayeux Tapestry's imminent Channel crossing</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260709-bayeux-tapestry-s-norman-conquest-story-crosses-the-channel-for-the-first-time</link><description>
Under cover of darkness and heavy police guard, the Bayeux Tapestry – a 68-metre embroidered chronicle of the Norman conquest of England, stitched in wool not long after the events it depicts – is set to cross the Channel within days, the official overseeing its move to London has revealed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0e3b1a0a-7543-11f1-ab2d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25265432520311.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0e3b1a0a-7543-11f1-ab2d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25265432520311.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c8a3f05e-7ad6-11f1-93c0-8f353acd979b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 11:17:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0e3b1a0a-7543-11f1-ab2d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25265432520311.jpg">AP - Lou Benoist</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>How appeal court verdict against Le Pen puts her back in the running for 2027</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260709-how-appeal-court-verdict-against-le-pen-puts-her-back-in-the-running-for-2027</link><description>
A French appeals court this week upheld Marine Le Pen's conviction for embezzling funds from the European Parliament and sentenced her to house arrest – something the far-right leader previously said would rule her out of France's 2027 presidential race. Yet Le Pen still has one last legal recourse to overturn her conviction and, pending that appeal, remains free to hit the campaign trail.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4fad30ec-796f-11f1-b128-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T210557Z-856145428-RC267MACOHTM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-FARRIGHT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4fad30ec-796f-11f1-b128-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T210557Z-856145428-RC267MACOHTM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-FARRIGHT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">262d088a-7ac5-11f1-8032-3f0e5d107485</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 05:09:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4fad30ec-796f-11f1-b128-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T210557Z-856145428-RC267MACOHTM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-FARRIGHT.jpg">© Tom Nicholson/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Le Pen confirms  presidential bid after Paris appeals court upholds conviction</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260707-appeal-court-upholds-le-pen-conviction-but-opens-door-to-2027-presidential-bid</link><description>
The leader of France's far-right National Rally, Marine Le Pen, said on Tuesday she would run for president next year after an embezzlement conviction was confirmed on appeal, a ruling she said she would challenge before the country's highest court.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7541e338-7a01-11f1-b036-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-07T124016Z-5387717-RC209MAY8HIE-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-LE-PEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7541e338-7a01-11f1-b036-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-07T124016Z-5387717-RC209MAY8HIE-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-LE-PEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c17a4c16-7a03-11f1-8629-8d930c9bc3ef</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 13:25:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7541e338-7a01-11f1-b036-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-07T124016Z-5387717-RC209MAY8HIE-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-LE-PEN.jpg">© Benoit Tessier/Reuters</source><dc:creator>Sarah Elzas with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>EU warns France under-15 social media bill could breach European law</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260707-eu-asks-france-to-revise-under-15-social-media-warning-breach-of-bloc-s-law</link><description>
The European Commission has warned that a French bill that would ban children under the age of 15 from social media would infringe the European Union’s online content law by giving French regulators powers that go beyond the bloc’s legal framework.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0fc5d478-6d5a-11f1-a9db-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B73U7CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0fc5d478-6d5a-11f1-a9db-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B73U7CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eee2fd10-79cc-11f1-a7eb-ef9ebc5c3f46</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 06:29:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0fc5d478-6d5a-11f1-a9db-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B73U7CQ.jpg">© Oli Scarff/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Marine Le Pen's presidential ambitions hinge on appeal court ruling</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260707-marine-le-pen-s-presidential-ambitions-hinge-on-appeal-court-ruling</link><description>
The Paris court of appeal is to rule Tuesday afternoon in far right leader Marine Le Pen’s embezzlement case, in a decision that could determine whether she can run for president for a fourth time, or if she will step aside. Several scenarios are possible, and her political opponents are preparing for all possibilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/54dae868-793b-11f1-bfb7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26185708599783.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/54dae868-793b-11f1-bfb7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26185708599783.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5e39e0d0-793b-11f1-82a8-836db58cffca</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 05:39:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/54dae868-793b-11f1-bfb7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26185708599783.jpg">© Jean-Francois Badias/AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's first diagnosed Ebola patient recovers after treatment</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260706-france-s-first-diagnosed-ebola-patient-recovers-after-treatment</link><description>
A French doctor who was the first-ever diagnosed case of Ebola in the country has made a full recovery and has been discharged from hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d195400-6fe6-11f1-b14c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-29T145943Z-1916668681-RC2XILA0ACED-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d195400-6fe6-11f1-b14c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-29T145943Z-1916668681-RC2XILA0ACED-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43821528-7945-11f1-9670-43701cbc316b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 15:31:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d195400-6fe6-11f1-b14c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-29T145943Z-1916668681-RC2XILA0ACED-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO.jpg">© Gradel Muyisa Mumbere/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's richest man Bernard Arnault ordered to pay €22.5m in back taxes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260705-france-s-richest-man-bernard-arnault-ordered-to-pay-%E2%82%AC22-5m-in-back-taxes</link><description>
Bernard Arnault, head of the luxury goods group LVMH, has been ordered to pay nearly €22.5 million in back taxes after a Paris appeals court overturned earlier rulings in his favour in a long-running dispute with the tax authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e6345d2-57e3-11ee-aae5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Arnauld%20Diner%20Charles.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e6345d2-57e3-11ee-aae5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Arnauld%20Diner%20Charles.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be08bdea-786b-11f1-a6cc-d36f21a515ea</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 13:06:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e6345d2-57e3-11ee-aae5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Arnauld%20Diner%20Charles.JPG">REUTERS - BENOIT TESSIER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'They've inflicted yet another assault,' parents say after judges mock mother</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260704-france-parents-say-another-assault-inflicted-when-justice-system-mocks-victims</link><description>
A mother who filed a complaint alleging the sexual assault of her young son said she was mocked by magistrates at a court in Bobigny, just outside Paris, after judges wrote that she had "overreacted". As Justice Minister Gérald Darmanin calls for an inquiry into the case, RFI spoke to the boy's parents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/68c46318-6054-11f1-b652-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4YF2CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/68c46318-6054-11f1-b652-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4YF2CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e283644a-747e-11f1-8cc2-432561169cd3</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 12:31:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/68c46318-6054-11f1-b652-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4YF2CQ.jpg">© Loïc Venance / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France reports sharp rise in deaths after record June heatwave</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260703-france-deaths-rose-by-30-percent-during-heatwave</link><description>
France recorded a rise of nearly 30 percent in deaths during the week beginning 22 June, the peak of the country's record-breaking heatwave, the public health authority said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/da0f433e-76a8-11f1-8e89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T220613Z-1012512868-RC2A5MADKJ7Y-RTRMADP-3-USA-WEATHER-HEAT-NEW-YORK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/da0f433e-76a8-11f1-8e89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T220613Z-1012512868-RC2A5MADKJ7Y-RTRMADP-3-USA-WEATHER-HEAT-NEW-YORK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">076ddfd0-76ad-11f1-aedd-518d93cbeb2e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 07:06:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/da0f433e-76a8-11f1-8e89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T220613Z-1012512868-RC2A5MADKJ7Y-RTRMADP-3-USA-WEATHER-HEAT-NEW-YORK.jpg">© Jordan Tovin/ Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France issues water safety alert after more than 90 drowning deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-france-issues-water-safety-alert-after-more-than-90-drowning-deaths-heatwave</link><description>
The French government said more than 90 people have died by drowning since 19 June, as authorities and swimming bodies stepped up warnings during a summer marked by intense heat and more people seeking relief in rivers, lakes, canals and pools.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28f3ca9e-7611-11f1-9b77-55a00649bc60</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 15:03:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg">AFP - ARNAUD FINISTRE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on France</category><title>Podcast: Adapting to heat, France's fitness boom, Paris Mosque at 100</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-france/20260702-podcast-climate-adaptation-heatwave-fitness-paris-mosque-algeria-france</link><description>
As France's record-breaking heatwave last week raises questions about how the country will have to adapt to a warming climate, we look at what that could mean for French culture. We also explore the country's growing interest in fitness – driven in part by its most popular YouTuber – and examine how the Grand Mosque of Paris, which marks its centenary this year, became both a symbol of Islam in France and a recurring source of political tension.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34686256-760a-11f1-bf8b-a7557f473b29</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 14:30:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sarah Elzas</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfires spread across southern France, as heatwave reignites forest concerns</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-wildfires-spread-across-southern-france-as-heatwave-reignites-forest-concerns</link><description>
Wildfires have broken out across southern France, forcing evacuations and stretching firefighting teams as the country prepares for the third heatwave of the summer, with the country's forests under increasing threat from climate change and disputes over logging.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76a15890-75f0-11f1-ae1f-a949136140ad</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 13:36:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg">AFP - LIONEL BONAVENTURE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris death penalty congress warns abolition cannot be taken for granted</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-macron-warns-death-penalty-debate-is-back-as-executions-rise-worldwide</link><description>
The fight to abolish the death penalty remains "eminently contemporary", French President Emmanuel Macron said as campaigners, judges and former death row prisoners gathered in Paris this week for the World Congress Against the Death Penalty, amid rising executions worldwide and renewed support for capital punishment in some democracies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f30e478e-7524-11f1-b65e-7129b96364f7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 09:44:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg">ASSOCIATED PRESS - Pat Sullivan</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France advances assisted dying law with strict rules and safeguards</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-france-advances-assisted-dying-law-with-safeguards-and-strict-rules</link><description>
France's National Assembly has approved a new version of a bill creating a legal right to assisted dying, bringing the country closer to a major change in end-of-life care. The legislation sets out who could qualify, how requests would be made and the safeguards designed to prevent abuse of the law. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">859a835a-7558-11f1-8d03-c36d4528ccb7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 06:05:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg">AP - Mosa'ab Elshamy</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France confirms dates for 2027 presidential election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260701-france-confirms-dates-for-2027-presidential-election-april-may</link><description>
France will hold the first round of its next presidential election on 18 April 2027 and the runoff on 2 May after the government formally approved the dates at Wednesday's cabinet meeting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0669c7d6-754d-11f1-af71-d16dd1da17f0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 14:41:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg">© THEO ROUBY / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French justice system to re-examine 88,000 child abuse claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260630-french-justice-system-to-re-examine-88-000-child-abuse-claims</link><description>
Some 88,000 complaints regarding sexual violence against children are being re-examined by investigative services – a figure higher than the 70,000 initially ordered by Justice Minister Gérald Darmanin last month. This comes in the wake of the murder of 11-year-old Lyhanna, whose death prompted public outrage over the state's mishandling of child abuse cases.
